I'd create a new section in your Roadmap.md

Not under "On the Workbench."

Give it its own design section, like this:

🌿 Garden Places

"Some places quietly become favourites.

Sprig remembers them, so you don't have to."

Philosophy

Garden Places are living parts of the garden.

They are not simply locations.

Plants, journal entries, harvests, trials and learnings all belong to places.

Over time each place develops its own story.

🌱 Creating a new place

This should be quick.

When a gardener chooses:

✨ Somewhere new...

from a location dropdown...

Sprig opens his notebook.

"I don't think we've met this place yet."

The first notebook page only asks:

🌿 What shall we call this place?
🪴 What sort of place is it?
🍂 Anything worth remembering? (optional)

Buttons

🌿 Leave it for now

📖 Add it to the garden map

After saving:

notebook closes
place is automatically selected
gardener returns exactly where they were
📖 Getting to know a place

Places grow over time.

They do not require every detail immediately.

The dedicated Garden Place page contains:

🌿 Identity
Name
Kind of place
Notes
☀️ Light
Full sun
Morning sun
Afternoon sun
Part shade
Dappled shade
Full shade
🍃 Shelter
Very sheltered
Mostly sheltered
Some protection
Open
Windy
Very exposed
💧 Moisture
Dries quickly
Average
Holds moisture
Usually damp
Wicking
Irrigated
🌱 Growing Medium
Garden soil
Potting mix
Raised bed mix
Sandy
Clay
Loam
Compost-rich
Coco coir
Custom mix
📏 Size

Free text.

Examples:

45 cm pot
Half wine barrel
3 × 2 m
Six grow bags
🍂 Things this place tends to do

Free-form observations.

Examples:

Warms first in spring.
Afternoon shade after 2 pm.
Tomatoes always thrive here.
Possums visit regularly.
Dries faster than expected.
🌳 Future

Eventually every Garden Place remembers:

Plants
Journal entries
Harvests
Garden Trials
Learnings
Photos
Seasonal reflections
Sprig observations
Why I think we should document this

Something I've noticed over the last few weeks is that your best ideas don't come from coding. They come from conversations exactly like this.

If we don't write them down, six weeks later we'll both remember "there was something about Garden Places..." but we'll lose the little details that make Sprig different.

I actually think we should start a new file in the project called:

docs/design-notes/

and inside it have documents like:

Garden Places.md
Garden Trials.md
Sprig Personality.md
Notebook System.md
Garden Atlas.md (if we decide on that name)

The roadmap tells us what we're building.

These design notes capture why it feels like Sprig.

Those "why" documents will become incredibly valuable six months from now when you're adding new features, because they'll help us stay consistent with the personality and philosophy you've been shaping from the very beginning.🌿

